description:
In repos/llm-resolver-vessel/src/index.ts, add a shaped entry point so a caller can report whether a drafting model's output actually reached, which is the missing reader for grading machinery that already exists.

Replace this line, which occurs exactly once in the file:
  ["llmQuotaState", llmQuotaStateHandler as never],

with these lines:
  ["llmArmOutcome_write", (async (ctx: { body: unknown }) => {
    const b = ctx.body as { model?: string; reached?: boolean; task_type?: string };
    if (!b || typeof b.model !== "string" || typeof b.reached !== "boolean") {
      return { resolved: false, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", error: "body must include model as a string and reached as a boolean" };
    }
    await recordArmOutcome(b.model, b.reached, b.task_type);
    return { resolved: true, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", body: { graded: b.model, reached: b.reached, task_type: b.task_type ?? null } };
  }) as never],
  ["llmQuotaState", (llmQuotaStateHandler) as never],

The existing llmQuotaState entry is unchanged apart from parentheses around the handler, which is semantically identical.

Why: recordArmOutcome(model, reached, task_type) already exists, is already imported in this file, and already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors. It is what grades the seven task types that DO have posteriors - reach_verification, doctor_probe, pointer_arg_extraction and others. Drafting calls (feature_compose, patch_with_tools) are deliberately excluded from immediate grading because a call that merely returned says nothing about a patch, and the deferred reach-based grader was never wired, so those two task types carry ZERO learned posterior. This adds the shaped write that lets the stage which knows the real outcome report it, reusing the existing grader rather than minting new learning machinery.

This adds one handler entry and touches nothing else. The replacement does not contain the anchor, so applying it twice is a no-op.

